# Japanese tokens are PRECOMPUTED at build time (scripts/precompute-ja.mjs runs
# on prebuild) into data/ja-tokens.generated.json, which is COMMITTED — deploy
# machines (Cloudflare/Netlify) never need Python. Python/Sudachi is only used
# LOCALLY at build time to regenerate that file. Install its deps once (see
# services/sudachi/requirements.txt); set PYTHON if your interpreter is not on
# PATH as `python`/`python3`. `npm run audio:generate` reads the same variable.
# PYTHON=C:\\Python314\\python.exe

# Reading, bookmarks, and preferences are anonymous and local-only
# (localStorage). There are no accounts and no database.

# Canonical URL used for absolute links in sitemap.xml.
# REQUIRED: `next build` fails when SITE_URL is unset in production.
SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ── Audio generation (authoring-time only: `npm run audio:generate`) ─────────
# Microsoft Edge's read-aloud endpoint through the edge-tts Python package: free,
# and there is NO key to keep or rotate. Install it once with the same
# interpreter the Sudachi script uses (see PYTHON above):
#   python -m pip install --user edge-tts
#
# PRIVACY: generating sends each sentence's text to Microsoft over HTTPS, at
# authoring time only. Readers never touch the network for audio — they play the
# static files under public/audio/, so CI and deploy machines need none of this.
#
# Speaking rate, as a signed percentage. The default (+25%) is deliberately
# modest: the reader already has a 0.5×–1.5× speed control, and a second
# speed-up baked into the file would stack under it. Changing the rate
# re-synthesizes — it is part of every cache key and of the story hash.
# EDGE_TTS_RATE=+25%

# `npm run audio:fixture` needs neither Python nor the network: it writes locally
# synthesized BEEP audio for smoke-testing the reader. Those manifest entries are
# marked "fixture": true, the reader badges them "Studio Audio · test", and `npm
# run build` warns while they are present. Run `npm run audio:clear` before deploying.

# ffmpeg is needed whenever something must be encoded — real runs AND
# `--fixture` runs (--dry-run needs neither). It is looked up on PATH first, then
# in the usual Windows install locations (winget/choco/Program Files), so a fresh
# terminal that has not picked up the PATH change still works. Set FFMPEG to
# override that lookup or to pick a specific binary.
# FFMPEG=C:\ffmpeg\bin\ffmpeg.exe
